    # ---- questions that must not be answered by random retrieval ---------
    (r"^what (?:is|does) gay mean\b|^what is gay\b|^define gay\b|meaning of gay\b", "**Gay** describes a person who is romantically or sexually attracted to people of the same sex or gender. The term is used by men and women, though many women prefer **lesbian**. Sexual orientation is not a choice or a disease, and using the term respectfully matters."),
    (r"which (?:gender|sex) is stronger|male or female.*stronger|stronger.*male.*female|men.*stronger.*women|women.*stronger.*men", "**Neither sex is universally stronger.** Strength depends on the task and the individual. On average, men tend to have greater upper-body muscle mass and grip strength, while women tend to have advantages in some endurance and pain-tolerance measures. Training, health, age and genetics matter far more than sex for any one person."),
    (r"men.*women.*genetic|genetic.*men.*women|male.*female.*genetic|genetic.*(?:male|female).*different|men.*women.*(?:differ|chromosom)|(?:differ|chromosom).*men.*women|sex chromosomes?|(?:xx|xy) chromosomes?", "**Genetically, men and women are far more alike than different**: they share about 99.9% of their DNA. The clearest difference is the **sex chromosomes** - most women have **XX** and most men have **XY**; the Y chromosome carries the **SRY** gene that triggers male development. Hormones (such as testosterone and estrogen) and gene expression then shape other physical differences, while natural variation within each sex is large."),
    (r"when was tensei\s*ai (?:released|launched|created|made)|tensei\s*ai release date|how old is tensei\s*ai", "**TenSeiAi v1** is the current local-first build of this project. It does not have a public commercial release date or version history beyond the build you are running. The version badge and model metadata in this app are the authoritative build information."),
    (r"when was one piece (?:released|first released|published)|one piece release date|when did one piece start", "**One Piece** began as a manga by Eiichiro Oda in **Weekly Shonen Jump on 22 July 1997**. The anime television adaptation premiered on **20 October 1999**. The 2023 live-action series is a separate adaptation."),
    (r"best (?:ai|artificial intelligence).*2026|which (?:is the )?best (?:ai|model).*2026|top ai.*2026", "There is **no single best AI in 2026** - it depends on the task. General frontier assistants include **ChatGPT (GPT-5-class), Claude and Gemini**. Strong open-weight families include **DeepSeek, Llama, Qwen and Mistral**, while small local models such as **Phi, Gemma-small and LFM** trade some accuracy for low size. For a specific job, compare accuracy, speed, privacy, context length and cost."),
    (r"what (?:is|are) the best ai|which ai is best|best ai overall", "There is no universal \"best AI\". Choose by task: **ChatGPT/GPT-5-class** for general use, **Claude** for long documents and careful writing, **Gemini** for Google integration, and open models such as **DeepSeek, Llama, Qwen or Mistral** when you want local control. Small models like **Phi, Gemma-small and LFM** are best when size and speed matter most."),

